# 7. RESPONSE UNITS — OPERATIONS STAFF VIEW

## 7.1 Purpose

This page allows Operations Staff to monitor the organisation's registered medical response resources and identify suitable units for dispatch.

It is an operational page, not a registration or configuration page.

Registration and administrative configuration belong in Administrator Unit Management.

## 7.2 Unit definition

For the MVP, a response unit is a combined deployable resource consisting of:

- An ambulance or medical response vehicle.
- Its assigned medical crew.

Treat this combination as one response unit for operational purposes.

## 7.3 Main page

Display these summary statuses:

- Available
- Responding
- At Scene
- Transporting
- Unavailable

Provide:
- Search.
- Relevant filters.
- List View.
- Map View.

**List View must be the default.**

Users can toggle between List View and Map View.

Each unit entry should display:
- Unit ID.
- Unit type.
- Operational status.
- Current location.
- Current assignment.
- Last location update/freshness.

## 7.4 Unit details panel

Selecting a unit opens a details panel showing:

- Unit ID and type.
- Registered medical capabilities.
- Current operational status.
- Current assignment.
- Last reported location.
- Location source and timestamp.
- Location freshness.
- Current activity.

Operations Staff may make permitted temporary availability changes, with a reason.

These changes must be recorded in the relevant audit history.

Operations Staff must not edit registration details, medical capabilities or assigned crew records.

## 7.5 Operational status rules

Use these exact statuses:

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Available | Unit can be assigned |
| Responding | Dispatch has been confirmed and the unit is travelling to the incident |
| At Scene | Arrival has been confirmed |
| Transporting | Patient pickup has been recorded and the unit is transporting the patient |
| Unavailable | Unit cannot currently be assigned |

System-driven status changes must be tied to confirmed events:

- Selecting a unit does not make it Responding.
- Confirmed dispatch changes it to Responding.
- Confirmed arrival changes it to At Scene.
- Recorded patient pickup and transport change it to Transporting.
- The unit becomes Available only after the response has concluded and it has been cleared for service.

Manual overrides require a reason and audit record.

### Important distinction

Connectivity and location freshness are separate from operational status.

A unit can be Available but have stale location information.

Do not label an unavailable location as live or assume that a unit is offline merely because its location has not refreshed.

## 7.6 Features excluded from this page

Do not build these for the MVP:

- Fuel management.
- Mileage tracking.
- Vehicle maintenance scheduling.
- Procurement.
- Crew shifts.
- Payroll.
- Driver performance.
- Advanced GPS analytics.
- Predictive unit allocation.

